{
	title: 'Rebase: rewrite a session history, append-only',
	spec: `A session's context can be rewritten after the fact: records dropped, prompt or assistant text edited, tool output replaced by a short note. Design: tasks/3zz/rebase.md (rows, actions, durable form, both clients); later rebase tasks follow it.
Durable form: one appended record { type: 'rebase', base: n, drop: [n...], edit: [{ n, text }], ts } and nothing rewritten on disk. replay.current applies the latest rebases in order, like replaces: dropped records leave provider input and the transcript, edited ones carry the new text. A dropped tool call drops its result and vice versa, so provider input stays valid; a turn's records are never split in a way the providers refuse (a tool result without its call, thinking without its signature block). Undo is another rebase that restores (an empty drop/edit list against the same base reverts to the records as written).
Compaction, clear, pruning, fork, find and lazy pages read through replay.current, so a dropped or edited record is gone everywhere except the raw file. The context graph marks a rebase as a cause (letter R). The record numbers n stay stable: links to #n of a dropped record show it as dropped, not missing.
Refused while the session runs a turn or waits on a question; the user pauses first. Applying checks base equals the last record number when the plan was built, so nothing appended in between is lost.
Old Hal reference: artifacts old-rebase.ts, old-rebase.test.ts, old-rebase-handler.ts (it wrote a new history file; here we append a record instead).`,
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Rebases project from the audit trail in record order; a newer plan with the same base supersedes its earlier plan, including empty undo. rebases.apply(id, plan, expectedBase) checks the current last written record; expectedBase defaults to plan.base and explicitly guards undo. Tool-result records with multiple results connect all their calls, and signed thinking connects its provider round. Rebased paging reads the audit trail to resolve cross-page groups and undo; ordinary paging remains bounded. Fork copies only projected records. Search rebuilds dirty sessions through replay, including unindexed fallback. Preserve prompt-replacement replay semantics when projecting before pruning to avoid applying replaces twice.'
	],
	needs: []
}
